WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.063
Unit 3 is the Microsoft traffic profile.

2
00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:07.449
It acquires Microsoft three
sixty-five and Entra I D traffic,

3
00:00:07.449 --> 00:00:12.187
and only this profile can; the
Internet Access profile never does.

4
00:00:12.187 --> 00:00:14.715
Enable it with Learn's Graph request,

5
00:00:14.715 --> 00:00:18.000
filtered on the m three
sixty-five traffic type.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.010
Then assign the pilot group in the admin
center, under traffic forwarding; the pages

7
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:27.512
the guide read give no Graph request for
the assignment, so it's a portal step.

8
00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:28.899
Then set signaling.

9
00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:34.525
Signaling carries source I P restoration,
so Entra sees the user's real address.

10
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:38.809
It's on by default only for tenants
that onboarded after June 2025,

11
00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:42.300
so the guide sets it explicitly
and records the state.

12
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.362
It's also the setting the
compliant network check needs.

13
00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:50.499
And Learn's caution: once Conditional Access
policies depend on I P locations or the

14
00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:54.072
